Second-gap transversal audit (codex-2026-06-03 S572)
==============================================================================
Goal: describe rows with M(S) < 2/(2n-1) in bounded primitive-box scans.
Test whether the real separator is perfect antipodal-transversal floor-tightness,
rather than coarse AP/sumset-minimality.

Primitive box k=3, max_speed=20, n=4, edge=2/7
  below_edge_count=1
  route_hist={'n_clock': 1}
  perfect_transversal_count=1/1
  flipsets={(): 1}
  sumset_excess_hist={0: 1}
    speeds=(1, 2, 3) n=4 M=7 Mval=1/4 route=n_clock perfect_transversal=True missed=- flipset=() sumset_excess=0 residue_count=3

Primitive box k=4, max_speed=16, n=5, edge=2/9
  below_edge_count=2
  route_hist={'n_clock': 2}
  perfect_transversal_count=2/2
  flipsets={(): 1, (2,): 1}
  sumset_excess_hist={0: 1, 1: 1}
    speeds=(1, 2, 3, 4) n=5 M=9 Mval=1/5 route=n_clock perfect_transversal=True missed=- flipset=() sumset_excess=0 residue_count=4
    speeds=(1, 3, 4, 7) n=5 M=9 Mval=1/5 route=n_clock perfect_transversal=True missed=- flipset=(2,) sumset_excess=1 residue_count=4

Primitive box k=5, max_speed=13, n=6, edge=2/11
  below_edge_count=2
  route_hist={'n_clock': 2}
  perfect_transversal_count=2/2
  flipsets={(): 1, (2,): 1}
  sumset_excess_hist={0: 1, 3: 1}
    speeds=(1, 2, 3, 4, 5) n=6 M=11 Mval=1/6 route=n_clock perfect_transversal=True missed=- flipset=() sumset_excess=0 residue_count=5
    speeds=(1, 3, 4, 5, 9) n=6 M=11 Mval=1/6 route=n_clock perfect_transversal=True missed=- flipset=(2,) sumset_excess=3 residue_count=5

Primitive box k=6, max_speed=11, n=7, edge=2/13
  below_edge_count=1
  route_hist={'n_clock': 1}
  perfect_transversal_count=1/1
  flipsets={(): 1}
  sumset_excess_hist={0: 1}
    speeds=(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6) n=7 M=13 Mval=1/7 route=n_clock perfect_transversal=True missed=- flipset=() sumset_excess=0 residue_count=6

Synthesis
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Every bounded row below 2/(2n-1) is already an n-clock-tight row with M(S)=1/n.
Every such row is a perfect antipodal transversal modulo 2n-1.
The bounded flip-set menu is exactly AP (empty flip-set) plus the known {2} sporadics.
Sumset minimality is sufficient but not necessary: some sub-edge sporadics have positive
sumset excess, so the sharper separator is floor-tight transversal structure.
